WEBVTT

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.200
It's time to go home.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.120
Students remaining on school grounds,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.870
please close all doors and
windows on your way out.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.400
Tamari...

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.780
You're...

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.660
...how pretty.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:47.690
This Boy Suffers From Crystallization

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.570
That Crystallization Syndrome's pretty scary, huh?

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.110
Your body crystallizes, right?

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.780
Thank god it's not contagious, amirite?

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.290
As if there's anyone who'd want
to be friends with a crystal!

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.870
Tamari Ayumu.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.520
It's Mr. Oni-chan!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.440
That's Mr. Onihara to you.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.180
I told you yesterday, remember?
You have to show up to class...

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.580
If you don't, you'll be held back again.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.320
H-How cruel of you, Oni-chan...

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.570
How could you say such a thing to a student

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.090
who couldn't graduate due to illness.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.360
Stop it with the fake tears.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.550
Tee-hee. You could tell?

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:52.790
Wasn't fooled for a second.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.500
But in class it's hard to fit in.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.600
Everyone's the same, except for
me. I'm older than everyone,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.180
it's awkward.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.010
I'm glad you're my homeroom teacher.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.450
So, anyway... Do you want
to touch my crystal?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.740
You're trying to change the subject.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.090
But Sensei, you like crystals, right?

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.620
What is it today?

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.590
...it looks like Caledonite.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.240
A blue with the south seas trapped inside...

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.240
To be able to view such
a beautiful crystal...

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.840
You're the only one who says that, Sensei.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.910
And that's why I like you so much.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.240
Stop being silly. And
start showing up to class.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.860
The talk-show yesterday, the latest
episode of the season's hit show...

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.930
The hip new app, the new store in town...

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.360
Conversation practice, and a character
lunchbox to spark things off...

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:06.970
...all set!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.930
- Good... morn... - Oh, yeah...

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.860
See that special on mascot
characters yesterday?

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.630
Sure did! This guy, right?

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.280
A giant salamander character!

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.280
Man, this character just cracks me up.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.410
T-They didn't notice me!
Man, this character just cracks me up.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.230
T-They didn't notice me!

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.310
Should I say good morning once again?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.310
But if they heard me the first time...

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.290
Would talking about the
mascot be more natural?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.480
Okay!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.660
G-Giant sa...

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.910
Oh, right... See the show last night?

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.570
How embarrassing!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.570
And wait, did anyone just see me now?

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.270
Do they think I'm shy?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.640
Did anyone notice I screwed up?

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.770
Phew...

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.900
No, this isn't good at all.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.990
I can't even greet someone.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.020
I'm totally hopeless.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.700
I wish I could have talked about
the mascot character, too.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.140
That's the bell.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.770
Take your seats.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.640
I'll take attendance.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.380
Let's put what happened behind us.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.910
We'll do better next time.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.920
Did you make that lunch
yourself? That's awesome!

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.620
Ah! Don't just take from it!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.270
Whoa, it's great!

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.160
Tamari, you're like a genius at cooking!

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.930
Come over here, eat together with us.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.340
It's a chance to talk to someone!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.730
S-Should I pick it up?

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.440
M-Maybe she'd think I'm creepy...

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.140
B-But... It's just picking up a pencil.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.380
- Here. - Thank you.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.730
Too late.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.650
Someone who can't even pick up a pencil...

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.450
Does she think of me like that?

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.660
Ouch...

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.360
Ah...

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:28.940
Are you okay?

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.910
Mr. Oni-chan...

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.780
Tamari, come with me for a bit.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.790
Earth Science Lab Office

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.790
Go on in.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.560
Just sit down anywhere.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.330
I haven't been here in a while.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.800
I see you've added to your collection.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:06:00.480
Ah... Your crystal today looks like this one.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:05.270
A type of quartz known as Phantom Quartz.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:08.810
It's said to have the power
to overcome difficulties.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.660
I wonder if he's trying to console me?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.620
You're so kind, Sensei.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.140
I love that part of you.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.140
Stop being silly.

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:23.140
Ow!
Stop being silly.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.300
Well, I'm feeling a little
better thanks to you.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.300
Tamari.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.390
Is it really so hard to be in class?

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.660
Today is the day is the day!
It all starts with a greeting!

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.020
Hm? Tamari?

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.070
What is it?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.570
I-It's nothing...

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.970
Man, that was so awkward!

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.890
What was that? It's nothing...?!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.980
After someone actually talked to me?!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.620
I changed my hair and clothes
to be more in style...

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:20.450
But if I'm still my same tongue-tied
self, nothing will help!

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.790
I thought if I changed my appearance,
I could change myself. But...

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:33.750
It's the grand opening of
Mermaidonuts in Shimashiro-shi!

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.170
The youth in town...

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.700
How to make friends

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.250
Are you okay?

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.940
Sensei.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:55.320
Tell me, where you can buy it?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.700
Saying good morning to each other...

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.680
Eating lunch together...

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.420
Shopping and eating on the way home...

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.680
Where can you buy that kind of youth?

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.160
I wouldn't know.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.170
Don't rub it in.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.140
Hey, Sensei.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.350
Console me...

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.080
I'll let you touch my crystal.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:18.910
I know!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.810
Falling in love with your teacher
is also a story of youth, right?

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.030
Don't use me to try and cover
up your feelings of wanting to

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.380
get along with your classmates.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.130
But, I really do...

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:35.480
You're fooling yourself.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.480
But... I'm crystallizing...

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.630
I got held back... I'm gloomy...

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.610
I'm sure no-one has a good impression of me.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.490
I want to talk to them,

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.570
but I keep thinking they'd be
bothered by someone like me...

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:59.960
Is there even a reason for me
to live when I'm so useless?

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.460
I keep thinking...

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:03.580
Silly.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:08.740
A sparkling youth isn't everything in life.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.000
There's no reason to try so hard.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.510
You're not useless.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.030
Just be the way you are.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.520
Stop going out of the way to
do things that get you hurt.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.610
Calmed down?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.200
Thank you, Sensei...

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:51.790
Well, if there's anything else,
feel free to come to me anytime.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.610
I'm always happy to listen
to your blubbering.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.110
Sure.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.090
Sensei...

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.120
Sensei...

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.140
Sensei!

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:17.480
alien rice balls

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.910
fried oysters
alien rice balls

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:26.940
Tamari.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:28.770
...hey.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.080
Sensei...

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:36.670
Do you...

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:37.220
Coffee in a beaker
Do you...

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.280
Coffee in a beaker

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.630
...have a girlfriend?

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:40.870
No.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.460
Oh, why not?

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.490
You're so good looking.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:49.340
I don't think I'll need one of
those for the rest of my life.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.920
Huh? Where are you going, Tamari?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:58.910
The school clinic?

00:10:58.910 --> 00:10:58.920
Ah... Yes.
The school clinic?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.870
Ah... Yes.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:04.880
Is it the crystallization?

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.270
I hope Tamari's okay.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.520
Just leave him be.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.250
Let's go.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.250
It has been a while since
you last crystallized...

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.690
I wish all group activities like
soccer would just disappear!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.090
Then what would be the point of school?

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.410
Sensei...

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.260
Do you want to touch?

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.300
It's been a while.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.880
It's like Tanzanite.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:46.200
It has clear lines, and is quite transparent.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:47.990
I'm gonna touch it.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.570
It's lavender, like the sky...

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:07.840
Tamari...

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:09.910
Pretty...

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.580
What?

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.210
What do you mean, what?!

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.000
Ever heard of boundaries?

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:19.800
Sorry.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.700
I got too carried away.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:26.060
My heart's pounding!

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.460
Tamari.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.540
I'm sorry.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:33.920
To apologize, how about I
take you someplace nice?

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:36.900
Someplace nice?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.870
Someplace nice…

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:41.520
Someplace nice... Like the hill out back?!

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:41.790
School Campus
Someplace nice... Like the hill out back?!

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:42.800
Hill Behind the School
School Campus
Someplace nice... Like the hill out back?!

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.660
Someplace nice... Like the hill out back?!

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.210
Where did you think I was taking you?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.660
I was thinking like out on the town,

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.920
some fancy shop... You
know... someplace nice?

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:54.130
Uh, no. Come on, let's go.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.960
B-But he said someplace nice...

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.980
I thought maybe it w-was, a d-date...

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:05.460
I even dressed up.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.540
I'm wearing my new shoes, and...

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.240
This is the pits.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.840
Tamari, close your eyes.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:17.980
Hey, what!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:18.980
It'll be fine.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.120
Hey, Sensei!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.650
I'm scared, what is it?!

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.850
Okay, you can open them now.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.960
Wow! They're so pretty!

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.680
It's like I'm in space!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.670
I had no idea there was a place like this.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.020
I told you it was a nice place.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:50.610
I call this place Stardust Garden.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.480
Mr. Oni-chan, are you perhaps
a romantic at heart?

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:57.480
S-Stop being silly.

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:58.990
You blushed!

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.060
You know, Sensei...

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:10.860
Ever since I met you, when
I hated crystals and myself,

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:15.210
I think that I've grown fonder
and fonder of them... and myself.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:19.140
So, thank you, Sensei.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.170
Y-You're just... so...

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.650
By the way, Sensei... Why do
you like crystals so much?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.780
Well, I do think they're simply beautiful.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:39.060
But looking at them also calms me down.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:44.380
Personally I think raw crystals
are far prettier than gemstones.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.370
The twilight sky, the forest green…

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.440
From the ocean's deep blue...

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.600
to a person's love...

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.170
Stones take hundreds and thousands
of years to become crystals.

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:00.520
And within them, they seal up
everything that's in this world.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.680
How could one not be
drawn to such brilliance?

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.080
And...

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.490
And...?

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.540
Crystals will never betray me.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.270
Stardust Garden, huh?

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:36.430
It was a really pretty place.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.170
I hope we can go there again some time.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:44.840
Here.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.360
Thank you, Tamari.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:48.860
No prob.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.550
I was having so much trouble
before, but now...

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:57.100
I just did it.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:06.060
Tamari, wanna eat lunch with me today?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.770
Um, I...

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:10.710
I don't care if you're crystallizing.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:11.710
Your lunch is amazing.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.430
grilled Isaki seafloor
rice
Your lunch is amazing.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:13.920
Can I try some?
grilled Isaki seafloor
rice

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:14.660
Can I try some?

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.420
Wow, it's delicious!

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.530
It makes you nervous picking up
a pencil for someone, you know?

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:29.370
Or asking to eat with someone...

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.500
You get nervous too, Shiraki?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.270
Sure... I mean, it's normal.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.880
I wanted to ask you sooner, really...

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.640
But Shiraki was all like we
should just leave him be.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.070
Because I thought we'd be bothering you.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:49.090
Everyone is the same as me?

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:53.620
Hello, Mr. Oni-chan.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.630
What is it today?

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.300
Listen to this!

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.570
I was asked to eat lunch
with Shiraki and his friend.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.340
Next time maybe I'll

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.850
invite them to this donut shop
that's all the rage lately...

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.840
You're still doing that stuff?

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:10.240
You're going to get yourself hurt
and crystallize more, are you?

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.220
I told you, don't push yourself.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:18.420
I'm not pushing myself.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:24.320
It's true that not doing
anything is easier...

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:30.180
When you said that, I did
feel a weight lift off me.

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:35.150
But then I would never move on, Sensei!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:40.210
Why should you put yourself in a
position where you could get hurt?

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:44.640
There are things more important
than not getting hurt!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.790
But your crystallization will get worse!

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.650
Sure, I'm scared of crystallizing!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:52.590
But it's better for my
body to become a crystal,

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.570
than for me to turn my own heart to stone!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.160
Wait...

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:04.100
Do you not want me to change, Sensei?

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:07.580
No...

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.600
I'm just... worried about you.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.390
Sensei... you dummy...

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:23.950
Damn it.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.980
What's wrong with living
with a heart of stone?

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:39.100
I don't want to be hurt anymore.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:52.880
Uh, hey... If you'd like, would you
want to go out for some donuts?

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.400
Sure!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:54.410
Yeah, let's go.
Sure!

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.580
Yeah, let's go.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.530
Sensei!

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:35.530
Sensei!

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:42.610
Sensei...

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.800
Sensei?

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:49.560
I'm sorry if you're angry
at me after what happened.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:53.670
But I have something I
really want to tell you.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:56.840
I've made friends.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.800
And I noticed something.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:04.850
Sensei, you said before my feelings
for you were just me fooling myself.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.620
But my friends and you,
they're totally different.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.250
Sensei, I...

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.190
...love you.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:19.550
I...

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.640
I don't love you.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:29.230
That's right. I'd rather...

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.010
I'd rather you be a crystal.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.380
I see.

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.040
I understand.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:15.820
Back to normal, I see.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.320
After I said something like that...

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.180
I wouldn't expect him to come.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:23.720
I hope Tamari's okay.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.830
I've sent him message after message,

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:27.780
but he won't respond.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.040
What is this?

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:43.570
When you see this note, please
come to Stardust Garden.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:49.090
If you really hate me, just throw it away.

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:52.420
What is he up to?

00:21:58.040 --> 00:21:59.160
Damn it!

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:08.150
Tamari...

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:12.210
Tamari...

00:22:14.590 --> 00:22:15.460
Tamari...

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.350
Tamari!

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:34.530
Sensei.

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:37.040
Why?

00:22:37.380 --> 00:22:39.180
You're crystallizing?

00:22:39.180 --> 00:22:41.500
I thought you were getting
along with your classmates.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:44.750
Is it because I told you to crystallize?

00:22:45.290 --> 00:22:46.250
No.

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.550
Then, why?

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.550
Because it was getting awkward between us.

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:56.040
But I wanted things to stay how they were,

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:03.040
Mr. Onihara, I, Tamari Ayumu,

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:07.400
think you're a bit timid, but a kind teacher.

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:12.040
And I love you.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.750
I...

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:33.580
don't care about you.

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:43.270
It would have been easier if that were true.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.420
I get uneasy when I think about you.

00:23:49.220 --> 00:23:52.730
I'm so scared that you'll
hate me or betray me

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:54.270
that I can't stand it!

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:56.780
If I could keep my heart a stone,

00:23:57.170 --> 00:24:00.280
then I'd be able to forget these feelings...

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:01.750
Damn it!

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:03.630
Then...

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:09.360
But, I might end up hurting you, Sensei.

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.040
You're the one who said there
were more important things

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:16.430
than not getting hurt.

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:21.270
Sensei!

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:23.500
Tamari!

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:29.290
<i>Back-to-back, we never come together</i>

00:24:29.290 --> 00:24:30.560
Sensei...
<i>Back-to-back, we never come together</i>

00:24:30.560 --> 00:24:30.910
<i>Back-to-back, we never come together</i>

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:33.790
<i>We go about our daily lives, passing each other by</i>
I love you, Sensei.

00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:36.370
<i>We go about our daily lives, passing each other by</i>

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:37.290
Tamari.
<i>We go about our daily lives, passing each other by</i>

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:37.720
<i>That story we always wished for</i>

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:40.290
Mr. Onihara…
<i>That story we always wished for</i>

00:24:40.290 --> 00:24:42.790
<i>That story we always wished for</i>

00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:43.360
<i>Carving out a puzzle piece that won't fit</i>

00:24:43.360 --> 00:24:44.640
Why?
<i>Carving out a puzzle piece that won't fit</i>

00:24:44.640 --> 00:24:47.560
First things first, you graduate.
<i>Carving out a puzzle piece that won't fit</i>

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:49.200
<i>Carving out a puzzle piece that won't fit</i>

00:24:52.110 --> 00:24:58.150
It's like the miracles
that rain down from the sky

00:24:58.280 --> 00:25:09.990
shine out their light like the
constellations watching over us

00:25:10.360 --> 00:25:15.990
If I could realize it was
so! I only had eyes for you!

00:25:16.110 --> 00:25:21.490
Agony, conflict, they're all
cancelled out by your smile!

00:25:21.610 --> 00:25:27.990
Decide one day on that glittering
wish, that dream you said

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:34.240
Why not? Even if I'm hurt in the process

00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:52.110
I wavered and hid it

00:25:52.240 --> 00:25:55.070
I only convinced myself

00:25:55.200 --> 00:26:00.740
So I'm going to tell you
everything I had bottled up

00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:04.070
I love the sound of your voice

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:06.700
I love your eyes

00:26:06.820 --> 00:26:13.440
It's flowing out, sparkling!

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:19.350
Since when was it like
this? I really understand now!

00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:20.700
Mr. Oni-chan!

00:26:21.070 --> 00:26:22.390
Thank you for everything!

00:26:23.030 --> 00:26:24.930
Congratulations on graduating, Tamari.

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:27.400
Thanks to you, I had a great
high school experience.

00:26:27.960 --> 00:26:30.270
And my Crystallization
Syndrome has been cured.

00:26:31.610 --> 00:26:33.400
Hey, Sensei...

00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:39.430
I love you, Tamari.
